00:18:09,385 --> 00:18:10,305
Qing.

265
00:18:10,385 --> 00:18:11,465
Qing.

266
00:18:11,545 --> 00:18:12,625
Qing.

267
00:18:12,705 --> 00:18:13,785
Qing.

268
00:18:13,865 --> 00:18:14,905
Qing.

269
00:18:25,185 --> 00:18:26,025
Mom.

270
00:18:29,065 --> 00:18:29,945
Mom.

271
00:18:30,705 --> 00:18:31,865
Mom.

272
00:18:37,545 --> 00:18:39,305
-Excuse me. Where's my mom?
-Don't… Don't come near us.

273
00:18:43,065 --> 00:18:43,905
I'm warning you.

274
00:18:44,505 --> 00:18:45,345
Don't…

275
00:18:45,425 --> 00:18:46,665
Don't try anything.

276
00:18:46,745 --> 00:18:48,505
What are you talking about?

277
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:50,625
Where… Where's my mom?

278
00:18:51,265 --> 00:18:52,825
You're worse than an animal!

279
00:18:53,345 --> 00:18:54,585
You have no conscience!

280
00:18:55,505 --> 00:18:57,185
You… What are you talking about?

281
00:18:57,265 --> 00:18:59,225
I'm just asking where my mom is.

282
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,825
Stop pretending.

283
00:19:01,345 --> 00:19:03,785
Before you passed out, you went crazy

284
00:19:03,865 --> 00:19:05,625
trying to tear the clothes
off my dad and me.

285
00:19:05,705 --> 00:19:06,465
We refused,

286
00:19:06,545 --> 00:19:08,425
and you nearly pushed my dad
off the cliff.

287
00:19:08,505 --> 00:19:10,185
His leg was broken.

288
00:19:10,265 --> 00:19:11,185
Then…

289
00:19:11,265 --> 00:19:13,305
Then you went to grab your mom's clothes.

290
00:19:13,385 --> 00:19:15,025
Your mom was frozen stiff.

291
00:19:15,105 --> 00:19:16,385
She wouldn't give them to you,

292
00:19:16,465 --> 00:19:18,225
and you pushed her off the cliff.

293
00:19:21,745 --> 00:19:23,065
No. That can't be true.

294
00:19:32,745 --> 00:19:33,745
Mom!

295
00:19:34,945 --> 00:19:35,785
Mom!

296
00:19:37,905 --> 00:19:39,145
Where are you, Mom?

297
00:19:39,225 --> 00:19:40,505
Mom!

298
00:19:41,105 --> 00:19:42,105
Mom!

299
00:19:43,785 --> 00:19:44,745
Mom!

300
00:19:55,385 --> 00:19:57,465
I passed out from the cold again

301
00:19:59,505 --> 00:20:00,585
at the bottom of the cliff.

302
00:20:02,825 --> 00:20:04,745
<i>When I woke up,</i>

303
00:20:05,265 --> 00:20:07,345
<i>I found myself in the rescue vehicle.</i>

304
00:20:09,145 --> 00:20:10,825
They found my mother's body

305
00:20:11,705 --> 00:20:13,305
at the bottom of the cliff.

306
00:20:34,065 --> 00:20:35,305
After the incident,

307
00:20:36,865 --> 00:20:38,425
my aunt took me in.

308
00:20:40,105 --> 00:20:43,945
<i>I ate, lived, and worked</i>

309
00:20:45,505 --> 00:20:46,585
<i>at her restaurant.</i>

310
00:20:47,305 --> 00:20:49,025
We got along well at first.

311
00:20:50,985 --> 00:20:53,545
But after the compensation money came in,

312
00:20:55,825 --> 00:20:57,065
everything changed.

313
00:20:58,025 --> 00:21:01,305
You jinx! Are you blind?

314
00:21:02,025 --> 00:21:03,345
There, there. Don't cry.

315
00:21:03,425 --> 00:21:04,505
You killed my sister,
and that still wasn't enough?

316
00:21:05,385 --> 00:21:06,665
Stay away from my granddaughter.

317
00:21:06,745 --> 00:21:08,145
Rotten luck.

318
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:09,385
Meeting you was the worst thing
that ever happened to me.

319
00:21:16,065 --> 00:21:17,665
Qing, are you tired?

320
00:21:19,985 --> 00:21:21,465
Look at you. Your clothes are soaked.

321
00:21:21,545 --> 00:21:22,385
I'll help you change.

322
00:21:22,465 --> 00:21:23,505
You might catch a cold.

323
00:21:23,585 --> 00:21:24,585
Catching a cold is serious.

324
00:21:24,665 --> 00:21:25,945
Hurry up.

325
00:21:26,025 --> 00:21:26,905
You shameless flirt.

326
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:29,545
I'll beat you to death. You witch!

327
00:21:29,625 --> 00:21:31,345
Shameless flirt! Shameless!

328
00:21:31,425 --> 00:21:32,465
Trash!

329
00:21:32,545 --> 00:21:33,345
Flirt!

330
00:21:33,425 --> 00:21:35,185
Witch! Witch!

331
00:21:41,745 --> 00:21:43,145
Qing, come here.

332
00:21:43,225 --> 00:21:44,345
Leave the dishes for now.

333
00:21:44,425 --> 00:21:46,345
Come. I have something to tell you.

334
00:21:46,425 --> 00:21:47,705
Great news.

335
00:21:48,785 --> 00:21:49,745
You've worked hard.

336
00:21:50,785 --> 00:21:52,905
I've found you a good place.

337
00:21:57,745 --> 00:21:59,825
She said she found me a good place,

338
00:21:59,905 --> 00:22:01,505
but really, she took someone's money

339
00:22:03,625 --> 00:22:05,425
and sold me away to be
a servant in another town.

340
00:22:08,585 --> 00:22:11,225
When I first met Yao Xincheng,

341
00:22:14,025 --> 00:22:15,305
I thought

342
00:22:16,185 --> 00:22:18,905
he looked like
a refined and successful man.

343
00:22:24,665 --> 00:22:25,905
<i>I thought to myself,</i>

344
00:22:26,585 --> 00:22:28,265
<i>my luck wasn't that bad after all.</i>

345
00:22:28,865 --> 00:22:30,825
Serving someone like him

346
00:22:32,025 --> 00:22:36,105
had to be a thousand times better
than staying at my aunt's home.

347
00:22:39,225 --> 00:22:40,185
NEW YORK BLOCK

348
00:22:45,945 --> 00:22:47,745
But I was completely wrong.

349
00:22:52,825 --> 00:22:54,745
<i>Yao Xincheng brought me to Yuanlongli</i>

350
00:22:55,705 --> 00:22:57,585
<i>to look after his father.</i>

351
00:23:19,465 --> 00:23:21,905
<i>From the day I met Yao Baiyuan,</i>

352
00:23:22,425 --> 00:23:23,745
<i>I finally understood</i>

353
00:23:24,265 --> 00:23:27,145
<i>what a true living hell was.</i>

354
00:23:39,265 --> 00:23:41,545
NEW YORK BLOCK

355
00:23:41,625 --> 00:23:42,465
Mr. Yao,

356
00:23:42,545 --> 00:23:44,945
I really can't do this anymore.

357
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:47,785
I'll find a way to pay back

358
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:50,065
however much you paid my aunt.

359
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:59,185
-Wait outside.
-Alright.

360
00:24:05,865 --> 00:24:06,865
Qiao,

361
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:09,265
I apologize on behalf of my dad.

362
00:24:10,145 --> 00:24:11,345
Given his current condition,

363
00:24:11,425 --> 00:24:13,025
I really can't find anyone else.

364
00:24:13,105 --> 00:24:14,505
I can raise your pay.

365
00:24:14,585 --> 00:24:16,425
As much as you want. Is that alright?

366
00:24:22,345 --> 00:24:23,705
I went to Weiyang Mall earlier today

367
00:24:23,785 --> 00:24:24,865
and picked out some gifts for you.

368
00:24:24,945 --> 00:24:26,145
Here. Take it.

369
00:24:26,225 --> 00:24:29,145
Mr. Yao, I really can't do this anymore.

370
00:24:40,985 --> 00:24:41,865
Five years.

371
00:24:42,585 --> 00:24:44,545
If you can take care of my dad
for five full years,

372
00:24:45,385 --> 00:24:47,105
I'll transfer the apartment to you.

373
00:24:47,905 --> 00:24:48,745
Alright?

374
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:53,225
Don't you want
a home of your own in Weiyang?

375
00:24:56,465 --> 00:24:57,985
<i>A home of my own…</i>

376
00:24:58,865 --> 00:25:00,985
<i>That offer was too tempting.</i>

377
00:25:03,385 --> 00:25:04,225
I was moved.

378
00:25:06,025 --> 00:25:07,665
So I forced myself

379
00:25:08,905 --> 00:25:09,985
to endure it

380
00:25:10,665 --> 00:25:11,625
and suffer through it.

381
00:25:13,185 --> 00:25:15,105
That's how I lasted a whole year.

382
00:25:17,225 --> 00:25:20,185
Maybe Heaven pitied me.

383
00:25:21,265 --> 00:25:22,865
At the end of 1996,

384
00:25:23,465 --> 00:25:26,385
Yao Baiyuan went up
to the 18th floor at night

385
00:25:26,465 --> 00:25:29,065
to peep at the Pattia staff

386
00:25:30,825 --> 00:25:32,385
and fell to his death.

387
00:25:34,225 --> 00:25:36,625
Qian Dajun knows everything about that.

388
00:25:37,585 --> 00:25:39,025
Yao Xincheng

389
00:25:39,665 --> 00:25:41,265
was a wealthy businessman
from another province.

390
00:25:41,825 --> 00:25:43,425
He was in overseas trade.

391
00:25:44,025 --> 00:25:46,665
His father was Yao Baiyuan.

392
00:25:46,745 --> 00:25:49,585
He had a strange illness.
He couldn't stand daylight.

393
00:25:49,665 --> 00:25:51,225
No one could cure it.

394
00:25:51,305 --> 00:25:53,105
In 1995,

395
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:55,025
he came to Weiyang for business

396
00:25:55,105 --> 00:25:58,625
and heard that the Qihuang Clinic
in our building

397
00:25:58,705 --> 00:26:00,265
specialized in rare illnesses.

398
00:26:00,345 --> 00:26:02,065
To make treatment easier,

399
00:26:02,145 --> 00:26:03,305
Yao Xincheng

400
00:26:04,345 --> 00:26:07,225
bought an apartment at New York Block
under Yao Baiyuan's name.

401
00:26:07,305 --> 00:26:09,105
He hired a maid.

402
00:26:09,865 --> 00:26:10,945
You don't know this,

403
00:26:11,025 --> 00:26:12,945
but Yao Baiyuan was a pervert.

404
00:26:13,665 --> 00:26:17,105
He had ways and means
to torment those young maids.

405
00:26:17,185 --> 00:26:17,985
Be serious.

406
00:26:19,465 --> 00:26:20,385
Alright.

407
00:26:20,985 --> 00:26:23,865
Well, no maid could put up with it.

408
00:26:23,945 --> 00:26:24,985
None of them lasted long.

409
00:26:25,065 --> 00:26:26,865
He was changing maids every week or two.

410
00:26:26,945 --> 00:26:28,265
In the end,

411
00:26:28,345 --> 00:26:31,265
every maid in Weiyang
refused to work for him.

412
00:26:32,025 --> 00:26:34,065
<i>Yao Xincheng could only</i>

413
00:26:34,145 --> 00:26:36,785
<i>pay high prices to hire</i>
<i>a maid from another town.</i>

414
00:26:38,025 --> 00:26:41,425
How did Yao Baiyuan die?

415
00:26:42,625 --> 00:26:45,065
That pervert got himself killed.

416
00:26:45,665 --> 00:26:47,225
He ran to the 18th floor to Pattia

417
00:26:47,305 --> 00:26:49,065
to peep at the girls changing.

418
00:27:29,785 --> 00:27:31,105
Help! Help!

419
00:27:51,185 --> 00:27:54,065
Does Yao Baiyuan's death
have anything to do with Qiao Suqing?

420
00:27:55,065 --> 00:27:56,225
Probably not.

421
00:27:57,265 --> 00:27:59,025
The police came too.

422
00:27:59,105 --> 00:28:00,345
His death was ruled accidental.

423
00:28:00,425 --> 00:28:02,265
Besides, whenever he went out,

424
00:28:02,345 --> 00:28:03,865
he always locked Qiao Suqing inside.

425
00:28:04,825 --> 00:28:06,145
After that accident,

426
00:28:06,225 --> 00:28:08,305
Yao Xincheng returned from overseas.

427
00:28:08,385 --> 00:28:10,985
It wasn't until after he dealt
with the funeral arrangements

428
00:28:11,065 --> 00:28:13,985
that he remembered
someone was still locked inside No. 415.

429
00:28:21,265 --> 00:28:22,305
Give me a hand.

430
00:28:45,585 --> 00:28:47,425
Mr. Yao was a filial son.

431
00:28:47,945 --> 00:28:49,665
He wanted to earn virtue for his father.

432
00:28:50,385 --> 00:28:53,785
So he kept his promise
and transferred that apartment to me.

433
00:28:54,505 --> 00:28:57,185
It was just that
he held foreign citizenship,

434
00:28:57,785 --> 00:28:59,825
and the inheritance procedures
were complicated.

435
00:28:59,905 --> 00:29:02,305
So he let me live there first

436
00:29:02,825 --> 00:29:06,465
and said he'd handle the paperwork
the next time he came back.

437
00:29:07,585 --> 00:29:09,385
I lived there for five years.

438
00:29:11,545 --> 00:29:12,665
By

439
00:29:14,465 --> 00:29:15,865
the winter of 2002,

440
00:29:15,945 --> 00:29:17,985
he still didn't have time to come back.

441
00:29:18,505 --> 00:29:20,065
I started pressing him about it.

442
00:29:21,345 --> 00:29:23,265
So he mailed me all the documents

443
00:29:23,345 --> 00:29:24,345
and told me to handle it for him.

444
00:29:24,425 --> 00:29:28,025
But by then, I wanted
to leave that apartment.

445
00:29:29,225 --> 00:29:30,625
So I sold it.

446
00:29:31,345 --> 00:29:34,385
Why did you buy it back in early 2003?

447
00:29:35,385 --> 00:29:37,665
At the time, I was working
at an insurance company.

448
00:29:38,745 --> 00:29:41,225
I dealt with a lot
of real estate developers.

449
00:29:42,905 --> 00:29:46,225
They all said housing prices
in Weiyang were about to skyrocket.

450
00:29:47,265 --> 00:29:49,345
Even though Yuanlongli
had rumors about a cursed building,

451
00:29:49,945 --> 00:29:51,505
and prices there wouldn't rise much,

452
00:29:52,025 --> 00:29:53,185
the location was still excellent.

453
00:29:53,265 --> 00:29:55,105
If it couldn't be sold,

454
00:29:55,625 --> 00:29:57,065
the owners could always wait
for demolition compensation.

455
00:29:58,105 --> 00:29:59,265
Later, I worked hard

456
00:29:59,345 --> 00:30:01,145
to get into the demolition department
of a property company

457
00:30:01,785 --> 00:30:04,185
so I could get
a bigger share of the payout.

458
00:30:05,705 --> 00:30:07,665
Why did you buy it
under Yao Xincheng's name

459
00:30:08,265 --> 00:30:09,745
and leave it untransferred
for more than ten years?

460
00:30:10,265 --> 00:30:13,425
Back then, there were always rumors
in the building

461
00:30:14,625 --> 00:30:16,425
that I was being kept by some rich man.

462
00:30:17,105 --> 00:30:18,585
I had no way to explain it.

463
00:30:19,105 --> 00:30:21,065
If the apartment showed under my name,

464
00:30:22,265 --> 00:30:24,345
there'd be even less way to explain it.

465
00:30:25,705 --> 00:30:26,905
Qiao Suqing,

466
00:30:28,025 --> 00:30:29,665
your story is touching.

467
00:30:31,225 --> 00:30:34,025
But it has nothing to do with my question.

468
00:30:35,905 --> 00:30:37,785
I'll repeat myself.

469
00:30:46,145 --> 00:30:48,305
How did you kill Xu Meng and her father?

470
00:30:50,425 --> 00:30:51,425
Officer He,

471
00:30:51,945 --> 00:30:53,385
I already told you.

472
00:30:53,465 --> 00:30:55,145
Their deaths had nothing to do with me.

473
00:30:55,225 --> 00:30:56,945
Did you see them again

474
00:30:57,465 --> 00:30:58,985
after the Mount Wu accident?

475
00:31:03,905 --> 00:31:04,745
Yes.

476
00:31:06,545 --> 00:31:08,065
I saw Xu Meng.

477
00:31:11,985 --> 00:31:12,825
Scissors.

478
00:31:12,905 --> 00:31:13,825
-Drink.
-Come on.

479
00:31:13,905 --> 00:31:15,305
What are you waiting for? Drink.

480
00:31:16,625 --> 00:31:17,785
-Again.
-One more!

481
00:31:17,865 --> 00:31:20,345
-Rock, paper, scissors.
-Rock, paper, scissors.

482
00:31:20,865 --> 00:31:21,705
Drink.

483
00:31:30,225 --> 00:31:34,105
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

484
00:31:36,225 --> 00:31:37,625
Pretending not to know me?

485
00:31:44,265 --> 00:31:45,985
We're pretty fated

486
00:31:46,065 --> 00:31:47,945
to run into each other in Weiyang.

487
00:31:48,905 --> 00:31:50,665
I came here to visit a friend.

488
00:31:50,745 --> 00:31:51,945
I'm leaving tomorrow.

489
00:31:53,305 --> 00:31:54,425
Lend me some money.

490
00:31:56,945 --> 00:31:57,945
I have no money.

491
00:31:58,025 --> 00:31:59,185
No money?

492
00:32:06,745 --> 00:32:09,065
Did you forget who you are,

493
00:32:10,025 --> 00:32:11,345
murderer?

494
00:32:12,425 --> 00:32:15,105
You pushed your mom off the cliff.

495
00:32:16,665 --> 00:32:18,065
Do the police know that?

496
00:32:24,265 --> 00:32:25,305
Wait.

497
00:32:30,105 --> 00:32:32,105
You're not staying
at a friend's place, are you?

498
00:33:26,465 --> 00:33:27,705
Nice?

499
00:33:29,505 --> 00:33:30,345
This…

500
00:33:31,345 --> 00:33:32,705
This was a gift. You can't take it.

501
00:33:48,305 --> 00:33:49,145
Thanks.

502
00:34:02,145 --> 00:34:04,385
<i>I had just crawled out of one living hell,</i>

503
00:34:06,305 --> 00:34:08,264
<i>only to be dragged into another.</i>

504
00:34:11,744 --> 00:34:12,784
Xu Meng

505
00:34:13,545 --> 00:34:15,824
worked at Pattia on the 18th floor.

506
00:34:17,025 --> 00:34:19,985
She kept knocking on my door,
asking for money.

507
00:34:20,065 --> 00:34:21,705
In the spring of 1997,

508
00:34:23,505 --> 00:34:25,065
there was a crackdown
on prostitution at Pattia.

509
00:34:25,824 --> 00:34:27,865
I thought I had finally broken free.

510
00:34:29,585 --> 00:34:31,105
But instead, she came even more often,

511
00:34:31,865 --> 00:34:34,065
saying she owed loan sharks.

512
00:34:34,865 --> 00:34:36,705
I had no money to give her,

513
00:34:37,304 --> 00:34:40,385
so she started taking things from my home.

514
00:34:40,465 --> 00:34:41,705
Until…

515
00:34:42,784 --> 00:34:44,705
Until I met someone.

516
00:34:46,505 --> 00:34:47,784
To be precise,

517
00:34:51,744 --> 00:34:53,385
he wasn't even human.

518
00:34:59,545 --> 00:35:00,665
Hold on.

519
00:35:05,065 --> 00:35:06,225
Thank you.

520
00:35:20,945 --> 00:35:21,785
Miss,

521
00:35:22,625 --> 00:35:24,785
sell your stockings to me.

522
00:35:25,945 --> 00:35:27,545
Name any price you want.

523
00:35:31,185 --> 00:35:32,305
I can help you take them off.

524
00:35:34,625 --> 00:35:35,745
Don't come near me.

525
00:35:38,545 --> 00:35:40,905
-Come on.
-Don't come near me!

526
00:35:44,785 --> 00:35:46,585
Later, I found out

527
00:35:47,265 --> 00:35:48,465
Wu Shanlong

528
00:35:49,145 --> 00:35:51,905
was the brother-in-law
of a rich businessman, Song Qingsong.

529
00:35:52,505 --> 00:35:53,865
He lived on the 17th floor.

530
00:35:54,385 --> 00:35:55,505
From then on,

531
00:35:56,025 --> 00:35:57,385
I hid whenever I saw him.

532
00:35:58,265 --> 00:36:00,025
But what was bound to happen

533
00:36:00,745 --> 00:36:02,665
was impossible to escape.

534
00:36:05,305 --> 00:36:08,545
I heard someone

535
